<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>2012/10 on Sebastian Korotkiewicz - Tech{{log}}</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/archive/2012/10/</link><description>Recent content in 2012/10 on Sebastian Korotkiewicz - Tech{{log}}</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 31 Oct 2012 10:42:48 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://sekor.eu.org/archive/2012/10/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Autostart in Linux - made easy</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/autostart-in-linux-made-easy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 31 Oct 2012 10:42:48 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/autostart-in-linux-made-easy/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://sekor.eu.org/images/techlog/rcconf.png" alt="rcconf" title="rcconf"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;add or remove programs from startup without effort, thanks rcconf!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;root@example:~# aptitude install rcconf&#10;root@example:~# rcconf&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>iptables simple ban ip rules</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/iptables-simple-ban-ip-rules/</link><pubDate>Thu, 18 Oct 2012 07:14:03 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/iptables-simple-ban-ip-rules/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ban an IP address &lt;em&gt;(IP address cannot be entered on the server)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# iptables -A INPUT -s 1.2.3.4 -j DROP&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ban an IP address &lt;em&gt;(cannot be accessed from the server on the IP)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# iptables -A OUTPUT -s 1.2.3.4 -j DROP&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delete Rule by Chain and Number&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# iptables -L --line-numbers&#10;&#10;# iptables -D INPUT 3&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flush a Single Chain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;em&gt;Delete all of the rules in the INPUT chain, run this command&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# iptables -F INPUT&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flush All Rules, Delete All Chains, and Accept All&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Convert ogg to mp3 and mp3 to ogg</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/convert-ogg-to-mp3-and-mp3-to-ogg/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 23:53:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/convert-ogg-to-mp3-and-mp3-to-ogg/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;install &lt;code&gt;sox&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;mp32ogg&lt;/code&gt; from you repository&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;convert ogg to mp3&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sox file.ogg file.mp3&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;convert mp3 to ogg&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mp32ogg musicsong.mp3&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Generate a checksum of the files in a directory</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/generate-a-checksum-of-the-files-in-a-directory/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 23:05:34 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/generate-a-checksum-of-the-files-in-a-directory/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;find . -type f -print0 | xargs -0 md5sum &amp;gt;&amp;gt; checksum.md5&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Change photos to pencil sketch in CLI</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/change-photos-to-pencil-sketch-in-cli/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 22:00:22 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/change-photos-to-pencil-sketch-in-cli/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;convert input.jpg -colorspace gray \( +clone -blur 0x2 \) +swap -compose divide-composite -linear-stretch 5%x0% output.jpg&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Play music on a remote computer via SSH</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/play-music-on-a-remote-computer-via-ssh/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 13:47:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/play-music-on-a-remote-computer-via-ssh/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;On the &amp;ldquo;music server&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sudo apt-get install openssh-server mplayer&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the your computer&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ssh &amp;lt;username&amp;gt;@&amp;lt;serverip&amp;gt;&#10;cd /path/to/music/files&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you want to play only one song&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mplayer song.mp3&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you want to play the whole directory&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mplayer *.mp3&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;In case of multiple extentions (example with mp3, wma and ogg files&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mplayer *.mp3 *.wma *.ogg&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Quick crontab man</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/quick-crontab-man/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 12:58:37 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/quick-crontab-man/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;#minute (0-59),&#10;#| hour (0-23),&#10;#| | day of the month (1-31),&#10;#| | | month of the year (1-12),&#10;#| | | | day of the week (0-6 with 0=Sunday).&#10;#| | | | | commands&#10;*/5 2 * * 0,4 sh /home/mod/script.sh &amp;gt;/dev/null 2&amp;gt;&amp;amp;1`&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Disable ping reply on GNU/Linux</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/disable-ping-reply-on-gnu-linux/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 12:37:56 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/disable-ping-reply-on-gnu-linux/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Disable ping reply temporarily&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;echo &amp;#34;1&amp;#34; &amp;gt; /proc/sys/net/ipv4/icmp_echo_ignore_all&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enable the ping reply back&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;echo &amp;#34;1&amp;#34; &amp;gt; /proc/sys/net/ipv4/icmp_echo_ignore_all&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Generating passwords in cli</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/generating-passwords-in-cli/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 12:29:20 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/generating-passwords-in-cli/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;-c = length of the password&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; /dev/urandom tr -dc _A-Z-a-z-0-9 | head -c10&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;generating random txt&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; /dev/urandom tr -dc [:print:] | head -c10000 &amp;gt; lol.txt&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Swap file creation</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/swap-file-creation/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 12:18:12 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/swap-file-creation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A simple way to add extra memory to your machine .&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Create an exchange file:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;dd &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/dev/zero of&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/swapfile bs&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;1M count&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1024&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;_The above will create 1GB file (1M _ 1024)*&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Improving access rights:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;chmod &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt; /swapfile&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Initialize it as a swap&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;mkswap /swapfile&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Activate &lt;code&gt;/swapfile&lt;/code&gt; swap space immediately:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;swapon /swapfile&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Make sure that it works:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;free -m&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To activate &lt;code&gt;/swapfile&lt;/code&gt; after Linux system reboot, add entry to &lt;code&gt;/etc/fstab&lt;/code&gt; file.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;vim /etc/fstab&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Add permanently to &lt;code&gt;/etc/fstab&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sh -c &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;echo &amp;#34;/swapfile swap swap defaults 0 0&amp;#34; &amp;gt;&amp;gt; /etc/fstab&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yes, just that&amp;rsquo;s it. From this moment we do not have to combine it with separate partitions, we can at any time enlarge/reduce the created exchange space (dd command).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Change all string on new im VIM</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/change-all-string-on-new-im-vim/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 12:04:36 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/change-all-string-on-new-im-vim/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;:%s/OLDTEXT/NEWTEXT&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;:%s/192.168.0.101/192.168.0.110&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Create GIF animation in CLI from images</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/create-gif-animation-in-cli-from-images/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 11:53:05 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/create-gif-animation-in-cli-from-images/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;convert -delay 200 -quality 20 -size 200 -loop 0 &amp;lt;images&amp;gt; &amp;lt;gifImage.gif&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;code&gt;convert -delay 200 -quality 20 -size 200 -loop 0 /home/images/*.png ~/gifImage.gif&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>scp - copy files over ssh in linux</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/scp-copy-files-over-ssh-in-linux/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 11:45:26 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/scp-copy-files-over-ssh-in-linux/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;scp filename.zip user@server:path&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;cd /home/dates/&#10;scp data.zip root@192.168.0.100:/var/www/&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>nmap - scan an ip range for a single open port</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/nmap-scan-an-ip-range-for-a-single-open-port/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2012 11:35:55 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/nmap-scan-an-ip-range-for-a-single-open-port/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;nmap -p80 192.168.0.0/24 -oG - | grep 80/open&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;[modinfo@arch-pc ~]$ nmap -p80 192.168.0.0/24 -oG - | grep 80/open&lt;br&gt;&#10;Host: 192.168.0.1 (router)    Ports: 80/open/tcp//http///&lt;br&gt;&#10;Host: 192.168.0.100 (aaa)    Ports: 80/open/tcp//http///&lt;br&gt;&#10;Host: 192.168.0.126 (nsa310)    Ports: 80/open/tcp//http///&lt;br&gt;&#10;Host: 192.168.0.133 (arch-pc)    Ports: 80/open/tcp//http///&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linux tar Command - Creating tar file via CLI</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/linux-tar-command-creating-tar-file-via-cli/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Oct 2012 11:24:23 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/techlog/linux-tar-command-creating-tar-file-via-cli/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="creating-a-tar-archive"&gt;Creating a tar archive&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar -cvf archiveName.tar directoryToPack/&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar -cvf archiveName.tar /dir1 /dir2 file1 file2&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar -cvf archive.tar /dir/music /dir/photos /dir/text.txt&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h1 id="unpacking-tar"&gt;Unpacking tar&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar -zxvf archiveName.tar&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can also unpack single files or directories using their list (divided by spaces) at the end of the command:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar -xf archiveName.tar file1 file2 dir1 dir2&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h1 id="packaging-the-same-file-formats"&gt;Packaging the same file formats&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar cvzf allphps.tar *.php&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h1 id="list-the-contents-of-a-tar-file"&gt;List the contents of a tar file&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;List all files in allphps.tar&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>